  "notes": [
    "Irregular reflexive -AR verb with an *o→ue* stem change (same pattern as *acordar*, *contar*, *recordar*): the stressed *o* becomes *ue* everywhere except nosotros/nosotras and the Pretérito Indefinido/Imperfecto/Futuro/Condicional, which stay fully regular",
    "Affirmative imperative attaches the reflexive pronoun with a written accent to preserve stress: *acuérdate, acuérdese, acordémonos, acuérdense*; negative imperative keeps the pronoun separate: *no te acuerdes*...",
    "Past participle: *acordado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to remember\" — almost always used with *de* before a noun: *me acuerdo de ti* (I remember you), *no me acuerdo de su nombre* (I don't remember his/her name); without *de* when followed directly by *que* + clause: *me acuerdo que llovió ese día* (I remember that it rained that day)",
    "Near-synonym of *recordar*, but *recordar* is transitive (no *de* needed) while *acordarse* is reflexive and takes *de*: *recuerdo tu nombre* = *me acuerdo de tu nombre*",
    "Not to be confused with its non-reflexive counterpart *acordar* (\"to agree on\"), which has the same stem change but a completely different meaning — see `Acordar.md`",
    "Related: *acuerdo* (agreement, noun), *recordar* (to remember — near-synonym)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/a/Acordarse.md"
